  <title>Flash messages</title>
  <p>
    Flash messages temporarily show Orca messages and command feedback in braille, then restore
    the previous display contents.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-flash-messages">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Braille</gui> category, <gui>Flash Messages</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Flash messages</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca shows messages and command feedback in braille. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Messages are detailed</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca shows detailed braille messages when a brief alternative is available. For
          instance, detailed command feedback might include both the setting name and its new
          value. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Messages are persistent</gui>: Controls whether
          flash messages remain displayed until the display is updated instead of disappearing
          after the configured duration. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Duration (secs):</gui> Sets how long
          temporary braille messages are displayed when they are not persistent. This setting is
          ignored when messages are persistent. Default: 5 seconds. Range: 1 to 100.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
</page>
